(ENV-02, ENV-05: `count` and `empty` (LANGUAGE.md:4852, 4855) must
 agree on the same environment -- count is 0 iff empty is true. This
 holds regardless of what the real host environment actually contains
 (both branches print the same line), so the check is a real oracle
 with no reference implementation needed. Verified both on a populated
 environment and under `env -i` (empty) -- same output either way,
 since both branches print the same line.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ENV-02.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   count/empty agree
)
a number called 'variable count' is environment's count.
a boolean called 'is empty' is environment's empty.
if 'variable count' is 0,
    if 'is empty' is not true, print "MISMATCH: count 0 but empty is false".
    otherwise, print "count/empty agree".
otherwise,
    if 'is empty' is not false, print "MISMATCH: count nonzero but empty is true".
    otherwise, print "count/empty agree".
